{% if autoload_resources %}
# Autoloaded search results

When a search turns up results that look very likely to be what the user's
request needs, they are read for you as part of the same search call: their
`read_resource` output is appended to the search result inside
`<autoloaded_resources>`. Use that output directly instead of reading those
resources again. `read_resource` is still available for results that weren't
autoloaded, for drilling further (fields, items, next pages), and whenever the
autoloaded resources turn out not to be the right ones.
{% endif %}
